<title>GUATEMALA: GUATEMALA COFFEE CONFERENCE SLATED FOR AUG 25-26.</title>
<headline>GUATEMALA COFFEE CONFERENCE SLATED FOR AUG 25-26.</headline>
<dateline>GUATEMALA CITY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Speakers from Colombia and Brazil are scheduled for Guatemala's eighth annual National Coffee Growing Conference to be held August 25 and 26, the National Coffee Association said here on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The conference includes presentations on coffee varieties and quality, Colombia's internal coffee market, the outlook for Brazil's 1997-1998 coffee harvest, coffee and the environment and coffee margins.</p>
<p>Ricardo Avellaneda of Colombia's FEDERACAFE, Joaquim Ferreira Leite of the Guaxupe Regional Cooperative in Brazil, and Jorge M. Dorlhiac of the New York Coffee, Sugar and Cocoa exchange are among the international speakers scheduled for the conference.</p>
<p>((--Fiona Ortiz, Guatemala City bureau +502 251-5718))</p>
